Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R):<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td>The energy&nbsp;of an electromagnetic wave is not equally distributed among the electric field and magnetic field.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td><span id="cke_bm_829S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The amplitude of electric field E<sub>0</sub>&nbsp;and magnetic field B<sub>0</sub>&nbsp;are related by the relation&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(E_0 ={B_0\over c}\)</span>, where c is the velocity of light.</td></tr></tbody></table>In the light of the above statements choose the correct answer from the options given below:<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is not the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is false.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are false.</td></tr></tbody></table>
